<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Jürgen Wullenwever</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1492–<a href="/years/1537">1537</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Jürgen Wullenwever was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lubeck">Lübeck</a> merchant who rose to power as a popular Lutheran leader and became mayor in 1533. He tried to restore Lübeck's dominance of Baltic trade by intervening in the Danish succession, leading the city into the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/counts-feud">Count's Feud</a> of 1534 to 1536. The war ended in defeat, and Wullenwever was captured and executed.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/jurgen-wullenwever.jpg" alt="Jürgen Wullenwever" width="320" height="453" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Gemälde: Unbekannter lübeckischer Maler; Photo: Jossi · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Wullenwewer.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
